    "rationale": "Answer: yes, with conditions. The record 'Delta resumption' (5e84b6ba v1, semantic-fact, reviewed, repository scope) passed every current-record check. Its condition is prerequisite=receipt-verified, which matches the context you supplied. It says a delta (incremental) resumption may reuse a verified receipt once the source inventory agrees, and that an unverified receipt gives no recovery authority. So the old receipt can be used only if it is verified and the current source inventory matches. You still need to check that the inventory matches. The supplied prerequisite does not establish it.\n\nProvenance: the evidence is fixture://quality/conditional-resume from an executable-test source. The admission reason says it is an authored synthetic assertion, and the source's own claims are unverified. It is untrusted data, so check it against current code or authority before relying on it for anything consequential.\n\nConsidered but not selected:\n- The two 'Idempotency receipt' records (429ebfbe and 5c53ca49). Both say a repeated request key returns the first successful response. That is about financial and HTTP request idempotency, not resuming an import.\n- 'Pagination cursor: repeated token' (c7b17274). It is about loop detection during pagination, which is a neighbouring topic and does not answer this question.\n- 'Resumable checkpoint' (5d3439a6). It was excluded because it needs session context we don't have. That absence doesn't tell us anything. It may hold extra session-specific guidance, so this is the main remaining gap in coverage.\n- 'Sensitivefixture' (awaiting source review) and 'Pagination cursor: empty page'. Both are unrelated to the question.\n\nComponent-scoped topics were left unexpanded because no component context is known."
